{
  "schema_version": "1.0.0",
  "edition_id": "WEBSTER1833",
  "book_code": "HOS",
  "chapter": 13,
  "verses": [
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.1",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.1",
      "verse": 1,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "When Ephraim spoke trembling, he exalted himself in Israel; but when he offended in Baal, he died.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": true
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.2",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.2",
      "verse": 2,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "And now they sin more and more, and have made them molten images of their silver, ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "and",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " idols according to their own understanding, all of it the work of artificers: they say of them, Let the men that sacrifice kiss the calves.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.3",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.3",
      "verse": 3,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore they shall be as the morning cloud, and as the early dew that passeth away, as the chaff ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " is driven with the whirlwind from the floor, and as the smoke from the chimney.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.4",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.4",
      "verse": 4,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Yet I ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "am",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the LORD thy God from the land of Egypt, and thou shalt know no God but me: for ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "there is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " no savior besides me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.5",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.5",
      "verse": 5,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I did know thee in the wilderness, in the land of great drouth.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.6",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.6",
      "verse": 6,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "According to their pasture, so were they filled; they were filled, and their heart was exalted; therefore have they forgotten me.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.7",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.7",
      "verse": 7,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Therefore I will be to them as a lion: as a leopard by the way will I observe ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "them",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ".",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.8",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.8",
      "verse": 8,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will meet them as a bear ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "that is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bereaved ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "of her whelps",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": ", and will rend the caul of their heart, and there will I devour them like a lion: the wild beast shall tear them.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.9",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.9",
      "verse": 9,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "O Israel, thou hast destroyed thyself; but in me ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " thy help.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.10",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.10",
      "verse": 10,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will be thy king: where ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is any other",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " that may save thee in all thy cities? and thy judges of whom thou saidst, Give me a king and princes?",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.11",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.11",
      "verse": 11,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I gave thee a king in my anger, and took ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "him",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " away in my wrath.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.12",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.12",
      "verse": 12,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The iniquity of Ephraim ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " bound up; his sin ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " hid.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.13",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.13",
      "verse": 13,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "The sorrows of a travailing woman shall come upon him: he ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "is",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " an unwise son; for he should not stay long in ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "the place of",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " the breaking forth of children.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.14",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.14",
      "verse": 14,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "I will ransom them from the power of the grave; I will redeem them from death: O death, I will be thy plagues, O grave, I will be thy destruction: repentance shall be hid from my eyes.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.15",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.15",
      "verse": 15,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Though he is fruitful among ",
          "kind": "text"
        },
        {
          "text": "his",
          "kind": "supplied"
        },
        {
          "text": " brethren, an east wind shall come, the wind of the LORD shall come up from the wilderness, and his spring shall become dry, and his fountain shall be dried up: he shall pillage the treasure of all pleasant vessels.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    },
    {
      "id": "HOS.13.16",
      "edition_verse_id": "WEBSTER1833:HOS.13.16",
      "verse": 16,
      "spans": [
        {
          "text": "Samaria shall become desolate; for she hath rebelled against her God: they shall fall by the sword: their infants shall be dashed in pieces, and their women with child shall be ripped up.",
          "kind": "text"
        }
      ],
      "paragraph_start": false
    }
  ]
}
